   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "policy_dependency_graph used to import the hotel corpus, so the abstract layer sat on the scenario layer. The\nprojection now lives in policy_demo_graph.py, which imports both sides; the graph module imports neither the demo\nnor its constants. Stack C is reached from :8083, so neither the graph nor the planner is an island \u2014 but nothing\nimports app/*, and app/* imports nothing outside its own package. That handover isolation is a different decision,\nnot this one, and it is still open.",
   "originalText": "policy_dependency_graph used to import the hotel corpus, so the abstract layer sat on the scenario layer. The\nprojection now lives in policy_demo_graph.py, which imports both sides; the graph module imports neither the demo\nnor its constants. Stack C is reached from :8083, so neither the graph nor the planner is an island \u2014 but nothing\nimports app/*, and app/* imports nothing outside its own package. That handover isolation is a different decision,\nnot this one, and it is still open.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true,
   "containerId": null
  },
